{
    "name": {
        "ara": "أَنْتُمْ فُرُوْضِيْ",
        "en": "Antum Furūḍī - You Are My Obligations"
    },
    "verses": {
        "ara": [
            "لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا اللهُ",
            "لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا اللهُ",
            "مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُوْلُ اللهِ",
            "عَلَيْهِ صَلَاةُ اللهِ",

            "أَنْتُمْ فُرُوْضِيْ وَنَفْلِيْ",
            "أَنْتُمْ حَدِيْثِيْ وَشُغْلِيْ",
            "يَا قِبْلَتِيْ فِيْ صَلَاتِيْ",
            "إِذَا وَقَفْتُ أُصَلِّيْ",

            "جَمَالُكُمْ نُصْبَ عَيْنِيْ",
            "إِلَيْهِ وَجَّهْتُ كُلِّيْ",
            "وَسِرُّكُمْ فِيْ ضَمِيْرِيْ",
            "وَالْقَلْبُ طُوْرُ التَّجَلِّيْ",

            "آنَسْتُ فِي الْحَيِّ نَاراً",
            "لَيْلاً فَبَشَّرْتُ أَهْلِيْ",
            "قُلْتُ امْكُثُوْا فَلَعَلِّيْ",
            "أَجِدْ هُدَايَ لَعَلِّيْ",

            "دَنَوْتُ مِنْهَا فَكَانَتْ",
            "نَارَ الْمُكَلَّمِ قَبْلِيْ",
            "نُوْدِيْتُ مِنْهَا جِهَاراً",
            "رُدُّوْا لَيَالِيَ وَصْلِيْ",

            "حَتَّى إِذَا مَا تَدَانَى الْـ",
            "مِيْقَاتُ فِيْ جَمْعِ شَمْلِيْ",
            "صَارَتْ جِبَالِيَ دَكّاً",
            "مِنْ هَيْبَةِ الْمُتَجَلِّيْ",

            "وَلَاحَ سِرٌّ خَفِيٌّ",
            "يَدْرِيْهِ مَنْ كَانَ مِثْلِيْ",
            "وَصِرْتُ مُوْسَى زَمَانِيْ",
            "مُذْ صَارَ بَعْضِيَ كُلِّيْ",

            "فَالْمَوْتُ فِيْهِ حَيَاتِيْ",
            "وَفِيْ حَيَاتِيَ قَتْلِيْ",
            "أَنَا الْفَقِيْرُ الْمُعَنَّى",
            "رِقُّوْا لِحَالِيْ وَذُلِّيْ"
        ],
        "en": [
            "lā ilāha illā Llāhu",
            "lā ilāha illā Llāhu",
            "Muḥammadun rasūlu Llāhi",
            "ʿalayhi ṣalātu Llāhi",

            "antum furūḍī wa-naflī",
            "antum ḥadīthī wa-shughlī",
            "yā qiblatī fī ṣalātī",
            "idhā waqaftu uṣallī",

            "jamālukum nuṣba ʿaynī",
            "ilayhi wajjahtu kullī",
            "wa-sirrukum fī ḍamīrī",
            "wa-l-qalbu ṭūru t-tajallī",

            "ānastu fi l-ḥayyi nāran",
            "laylan fa-bashshartu ahlī",
            "qultu mkuthū fa-laʿallī",
            "ajid hudāya laʿallī",

            "danawtu minhā fa-kānat",
            "nāra l-mukallami qablī",
            "nūdītu minhā jihāran",
            "ruddū layāliya waṣlī",

            "ḥattā idhā mā tadāna l-",
            "mīqātu fī jamʿi shamlī",
            "ṣārat jibāliya dakkan",
            "min haybati l-mutajallī",

            "wa-lāḥa sirrun khafiyyun",
            "yadrīhi man kāna mithlī",
            "wa-ṣirtu Mūsā zamānī",
            "mudh ṣāra baʿḍiya kullī",

            "fa-l-mawtu fīhi ḥayātī",
            "wa-fī ḥayātiya qatlī",
            "ana l-faqīru l-muʿannā",
            "riqqū li-ḥālī wa-dhullī"
        ]
    },
    "translation": {
        "en": [
            "There is no god but Allah",
            "There is no god but Allah",
            "Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,",
            "upon him be the blessings of Allah.",

            "You are my obligations and my voluntary acts,",
            "you are my talk and what occupies me.",
            "O my qibla in my prayer",
            "when I stand to pray,",

            "your beauty is set before my eyes;",
            "towards it I have turned my whole being.",
            "Your secret is in my innermost heart,",
            "and the heart is the Mount of divine disclosure.",

            "I glimpsed a fire in the encampment",
            "by night, and gave my people the good news.",
            "I said, “Stay here, for perhaps",
            "I may find my guidance there, perhaps.”",

            "I drew near to it, and it was",
            "the fire of the one spoken to before me.",
            "I was called from it openly:",
            "“Bring back the nights of my union.”",

            "Until, when the appointed time",
            "drew near for my union,",
            "my mountains were crushed to dust",
            "in awe of the One who disclosed Himself.",

            "A hidden secret shone out",
            "which only one like me can know.",
            "I became the Moses of my time",
            "since my part became my whole.",

            "In death is my life,",
            "and in my life is my slaying.",
            "I am the poor one, worn by love’s pain;",
            "have pity on my state and my lowliness."
        ]
    },
